<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Data extraction rules for Android 12+ (API 31+). For older versions it is backup_rules.xml, which must be
   edited IN SYNC: the project's minSdk is 24, so both files really are in effect.

   Two different reasons to exclude something, and they must not be confused:

   1. secure_settings.xml is about CORRECTNESS, not privacy. The file belongs to
      EncryptedSharedPreferences (SettingsRepository) and is encrypted with a key from the Android Keystore,
      and the Keystore is NEVER backed up or transferred. A file restored on another device cannot be
      decrypted, and EncryptedSharedPreferences.create throws on the very first access. That access is the
      API key read in the LLM chain, so the agent was dead right after a move, and only "clear data" cured
      it. Excluded from BOTH channels.

   2. The ai_open_pocket_db database is about PRIVACY. It holds the whole chat history and all of the
      agent's memory, in plain text. For an app with a local AI, sending it to Google's cloud backup is out
      of place, so cloud-backup does not take it. Device-transfer (a direct move to a new device that the
      user starts themselves) keeps it: the data does not go to someone else's servers, and a move does
      not cost the user all their conversations.

   3. The agent's files are the same PRIVACY as the database, with the same rule (cloud — no, transfer — yes):
      - agent/ and agents/ are the file_tool sandboxes (plain chat and agents' own folders): notes, a diary,
        exports, everything the agent wrote down about the user;
      - lesson_images/ are lesson images, including "Draw it for me" ones drawn from "about me".
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="secure_settings.xml"/>
        <exclude domain="database" path="ai_open_pocket_db"/>
        <exclude domain="database" path="ai_open_pocket_db-wal"/>
        <exclude domain="database" path="ai_open_pocket_db-shm"/>
        <exclude domain="file" path="agent"/>
        <exclude domain="file" path="agents"/>
        <exclude domain="file" path="lesson_images"/>
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="secure_settings.xml"/>
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
